  "rootCreativeReview": {
    "motif-ecologies": "A coherent open-centered rosette population, interchangeable rings on identical sites, a deliberately sparse ring fragment and a dense slanted dot ribbon. Width 600 and population cap 400 exercised exact values outside the slider intervals.",
    "contour-scores": "A stitched noise landscape, continuous ink on the same paths, beaded hill contours and an open saddle gesture. The material changes are distinct from threshold/source construction.",
    "region-quilts": "Mixed fillers establish hierarchy; wave-filled leaves expose local source fitting; bead/rosette substitution reaches three nested levels; beaded islands and sparse hatch fragments leave useful negative space. Very thin leaves can legitimately read as lines.",
    "layered": "Root inspected all three final pairs in both orders. Filled discs replaced the exploratory all-outline ring pair to make fill-versus-line contrast and foreground order stronger. Meadow/terrain and archipelago/gesture intentionally have subtler crossing effects.",
    "limits": "Scoped admission of the three studies and reviewed compositions, not a claim that every setting or the rest of the gallery is artistically accepted. Slider intervals are authored working spans, not universally measured quality ranges."
  },
